{# Table of contents partial (Feature f048).
   Include in any template: {% include "toc.html.jinja" %}
   Requires page.toc in the template context.

   Two renderings, chosen by scale (yqr-b038). A page with a prose-sized
   outline gets the full nested list. A long document -- the mounted
   changelog is the live case: 16 releases times their Added/Fixed
   subsections made 56 entries, 1700px of list before any content -- gets
   a compact index instead: top-level entries only, flowing as wrapped
   chips. The threshold is over the chip form's own row capacity, so a
   page never gets the compact form without needing it; the mount cannot
   carry frontmatter, which is why the rule is scale, not configuration. #}
{% if page.toc %}
{% if page.toc | length > 12 %}
<nav class="toc toc-compact" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <h4>On this page</h4>
    <ul>
    {% for entry in page.toc %}
        {% if entry.level <= 2 %}
        <li><a href="#{{ entry.id }}">{{ entry.text }}</a></li>
        {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</nav>
{% else %}
<nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <h4>On this page</h4>
    <ul>
    {% for entry in page.toc %}
        <li class="toc-level-{{ entry.level }}">
            <a href="#{{ entry.id }}">{{ entry.text }}</a>
        </li>
    {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</nav>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
